														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1362102">
									

<p>Something else you might want to clear up: when an actual EMP fries electronics, they are quite literally fried. They don't just turn off temporarily and turn back on later like in every movie ever. You might want to specify that the electronics are only temporarily disrupted. Granted, you said radio wave, not EMP wave, so maybe you already know everything I just said and I just don't know that radio waves can temporarily disable electronics. In that case, feel free to ignore everything up there.</p>
<p>But in other news, you should totally make the packaging look like a missle silo. And include a plastic stand that looks like a genuine missle-launching stand thing so that kids can fire it at their neighbors rather than just sending it straight up.</p>
<p>Edit: Now that my childish glee has worn off and I've had time to think about it, I've realized that Wondertainment probably wouldn't include the stand. That would be very unsafe, and the last thing Wondertainment wants is for kids to be unsafe.</p>

							</div>

								
