<p>Seconding what Anaxagoras said, this thing is too destructive in its current form. Each one of these things wiping out electronics for <em>miles</em>? Simply doesn't compute.</p>
<p>Here's how I'd tweak things:</p>
<p>The 'extremely bright light' is the size of a pinpoint. If you're looking exactly at it, it's as dangerous as a real one to someone's vision. But otherwise, it's non-harmful. <em>But wear eye protection anyway, kids!</em></p>
<p>The sound? Loud, but not drastically so. Might give headaches.</p>
<p>The 'emp wipeout range'? Drastically reduced. Safe to 'bomb' on your lawn, but not inside, kids!</p>
<p>Right now, I have to downvote.</p>

