			<div class="content" id="post-content-1362286">
									

<p>Thanks for the criticism. I'll try to address it.</p>
<p>@Request/Denial: Changed to reflect criticism. Request is now to inform governments <em>preemptively</em> of SCP-1068. The O5 denial has been removed.</p>
<p>@Destructive Potential: I understand that a giant flashbang/temporary electronic wipeout/giant BOOM! sound is a bit over-the-top for a Wondertainment product. The key here, however, is that the object is a fake nuke that when detonated, resembles a nuclear device to both kids and world governments. Reducing the size of the light means that it'll obviously be detected as a fake. Reducing the sound is easier, but still reduces the overall illusion (Maybe the sound starts a few kilometers away and is quieter from there?). And the pulse I intentionally kept vague on the size of, since a radius of 1 kilometer isn't really that big, and a radius of 9 kilometers is pretty damn big.</p>
<p>Maybe it should come packaged with a pair of goggles/earplugs that block all sound/light the moment the model detonates? It would show that Wondertainment cares about the safety of the kids buying their products, while still showing a complete accidental disregard for everything else.</p>
<p>@Seems more Factory than Wondertainment: In my experience, factory items are generally smaller, less toy-like, and are more gruesome for the user/victim. If it still seems like a Factory item to you, please tell me what parts seem more Factory-like to you.</p>

							</div>

								
					
